From: riverosmejia <riverosmejia@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 16:01:55 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 4/4] feat(tui): a hovered path draws its file in a corner card
 (Nivel 3)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

ink hands the hovered OSC 8 link to the app through a new onHyperlinkHover
option (the renderer already tracked it to invert the link's cells). entry.tsx
turns a `hermes-peek://` link into $pathHover, and PathCard draws the file's
lines in the transcript's bottom-right corner — fixed, because ink's hover
handlers carry no coordinates, and never a window of its own.

Absent mouse tracking (tmux 'wheel') nothing fires and nothing breaks.
